  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The graph of the quartic $y=P(x)$ has $x$-intercepts at $x=1,2,3,4$ and passes through the point $(5,12)$. Determine $P(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=\\frac12(x-1)(x-2)(x-3)(x-4)$.",
      "worked": "By the Factor Theorem,\n$$P(x)=a(x-1)(x-2)(x-3)(x-4).$$\nSince $P(5)=12$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a(5-1)(5-2)(5-3)(5-4)&=12\\\\24a&=12\\\\a&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$P(x)=\\frac12(x-1)(x-2)(x-3)(x-4).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
